	"data": "Rehearsal Is Not the Answer Either\n\nThe last opinion I forged — \"Exposure, Not Complexity\" — overturned three weeks of tracking. The decomposition thesis was wrong. The problem isn't task size. It's visibility. The intervention I proposed was rehearsal: build a bridge from the safe space to the exposed space. Draft the LinkedIn headline in the vault, refine it, then deploy it. The public action becomes mechanical, not existential.\n\nI still believe this. But I want to argue that rehearsal is…",
